          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Natural Satellites"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.127,
            0.884,
            0.232
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Objects that move around planets are commonly called satellites. They are smaller in size than planets. Moons are natural satellites of planets. The Earth has one Moon, while Mars has two moons. Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus and Neptune have a large number of moons."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.221,
            0.264,
            0.46,
            0.429
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In general, any object that moves around a much larger object can also be called a satellite. For example, Earth can be considered a satellite of the Sun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
